## ***********************************************************************
## **
## **  GPB.INC.BL -- the GP.BASIC keyword definitions for BASLOAD.
## **
## **  #INCLUDE it at the top of any BASL source using GP keywords. BASLOAD
## **  knows the ROM's keywords only; this teaches it the GP ones.
## **
## **  The keywords themselves are documented in GPC-BASIC/GP-BASIC.md.
## **
## **  WARNING: the byte values are the ABI. They mirror getGP() in
## **  source/common-scripts/c64tokens.py exactly -- $CE7F down, one per
## **  keyword, allocated downward and never renumbered. A keyword added
## **  there is added here in the same change.
## **
## **  A PRG holding these keywords is compile-only. Nothing in BASIC sits
## **  behind $CE7x, so the ROM can neither LIST nor RUN it.
## **
## ***********************************************************************
#IFNDEF GP.DEFS
#DEFINE GP.DEFS 1

## ---- loops ----
#TOKEN GP.DO 52863
#TOKEN GP.LOOP 52862
#TOKEN GP.EXITDO 52861

## ---- machine code, and SYS's own result words ----
#TOKEN GP.CALL 52860
#TOKEN GP.A 52859
#TOKEN GP.X 52858
#TOKEN GP.Y 52857
#TOKEN GP.C 52856

## ---- strings ----
#TOKEN GP.INSTR 52855
#TOKEN GP.STRPTR 52854

## ---- case-blind compare ----
#TOKEN GP.COMP 52848

## ---- arrays ----
#TOKEN GP.ARRPTR 52846

## ---- drawing, straight into VERA ----
#TOKEN GP.BOX 52843
#TOKEN GP.FILL 52842
#TOKEN GP.CHAR 52824
#TOKEN GP.PRINTAT 52841

## ---- select ----
#TOKEN GP.SELECT 52838
#TOKEN GP.CASE 52837
#TOKEN GP.OTHER 52836
#TOKEN GP.ENDSEL 52835

## ---- a region that runs from a RAM bank ----
#TOKEN GP.BANKED 52823
#TOKEN GP.ENDBANKED 52822

## ---- banked text: GP.BANKEDSTR <bank> <name> ... GP.ENDBANKEDSTR, read with
## ---- GP.BSTR(<name>,n). GP.BSTRCOUNT(<name>) is the group's size, a compile-time
## ---- constant. The body lines are BARE QUOTED STRINGS, not REMs: BASLOAD upper-cases
## ---- REM text and would destroy the case of every string.
#TOKEN GP.BSTR 52821
#TOKEN GP.BSTRCOUNT 52820
#TOKEN GP.BANKEDSTR 52819
#TOKEN GP.ENDBANKEDSTR 52818

## ---- block if ----
#TOKEN GP.IF 52830
#TOKEN GP.ELSEIF 52829
#TOKEN GP.ELSE 52828
#TOKEN GP.ENDIF 52827

## ---- inline assembly ----
#TOKEN GP.ASM 52826
#TOKEN GP.ENDASM 52825

## ---- predicates and byte splitting ----
#TOKEN GP.CONTAINS 52834
#TOKEN GP.HIBYTE 52833
#TOKEN GP.LOBYTE 52832
#TOKEN GP.ISEMPTY 52831

#ENDIF
